==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Plug Suit Asuka''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Eyepatch Li'l Asuka''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Asuka can be really good if you happen to get her early on, as she is strong against Red and has Area Attack. Her DPS is also very high, so she is a good counter to early game Red enemies like [[Sir Seal]] and [[One Horn]]. She is also good in early/middle [[Stories of Legend]] stages, as she can tank and take out close-ranged enemies like [[Bore]], [[Shy Boy]], and [[J.K. Bun Bun|J.K. Bun Bun]]. It is recommended you only use her for Red enemies, as her stats will not be enough to carry her in tough generalist stages like [[Overachiever Central]] or [[Technocracy]].

It is worth noting that she faces pretty fierce competition from [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], who both has much more health and a much quicker recharge time than her. Unless the stage demands her damage output, or her range is needed to stay safe from non-Red attacks, you're likely better off just using Roe Cat.

==='''True Form'''===
Eyepatch Li'l Asuka gains the ability to knockback Red enemies. Unfortunately, this niche is already occupied by [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]], who is more spammable than her and has the side niche of being a [[Immune to Waves|wave immune]] meatshield via [[Talents]]. While there are some situations where she has an edge over Pirate Cat, like against [[Capy|Capies]], it shouldn't be relied upon - you're better off treating this ability as a bonus when using her. Other than that, her stat change is very minimal.

